; 					&lt;td style="width: 69.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 20.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;40,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 2.7pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 43.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;30&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 2.7pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 97.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: left"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;September&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;30, 2055&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 2.7pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: left"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 51.7pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;5.90&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 0"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 42.1pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 12.1pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 14.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 12.05pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 16.65pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 81.55pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 13.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 55.15pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 13.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 110.3pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 13.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.85pt"&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 27pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Series A Notes are subject to scheduled amortization payments beginning March 31, 2026, as specified in the Note Purchase Agreement. The remaining principal balance of Series A and the principal balance of Series B-D of the Senior Notes Facility will be due and payable on the stated maturity date. Interest is payable semi-annually on March 31 and September 30 of each year, commencing on March 31, 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;In 2025, the company recognized $4.1 million in interest expense related to the Note Purchase Agreement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Under the Note Purchase Agreement, the Company can voluntarily prepay the notes of any Series in whole or in part. The Company is required to provide written notice of each prepayment and to pay a make-whole amount equal to the excess, if any, of the discounted value of the remaining scheduled payments over the amount of the called principal and including unpaid interest accrued.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.7pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;(c)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 15.14pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;New Credit Agreement&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.7pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On August 28, 2025, the Company executed a new credit agreement with a group of lenders (New Credit Agreement). The New Credit Agreement includes a $10.0 million revolving and letter of credit facility to fund working capital expenditures and for other general corporate purposes and issuances of letters of credit.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The New Credit Agreement specifies a maturity date as August 28, 2030. All loans are due and payable at the maturity date. Voluntary pre payments prior to the maturity date are provided for in the New Credit Agreement but such prepayments are not mandatory.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;LS Power Grid New York Holdings, LLC agreed to secure all the Company's obligations under the Note Purchase Agreement and the New Credit Agreement by granting to The Bank of New York Mellon, as Collateral Agent, a first priority lien on 100% of its equity interests in the Company. The collateral secures the Notes on a pari passu basis with the obligations under the New Credit Agreement, as governed by the Collateral Agency and Intercreditor Agreement dated August 28, 2025.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The New Credit Agreement references the Common Terms Agreement, which requires compliance with affirmative and negative covenants, including, among other things, financial statement reporting requirements and limitations or restrictions relating to the use of the proceeds, additional indebtedness and disposition of assets. The Company is in compliance with all covenants at December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;A commitment fee equal to 0.1% per annum on the unused portion of the Revolving Loan Facility is payable quarterly until the commitments are terminated. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company incurred total commitment fees of $4 thousand.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.7pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;(d)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.52pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;Common Terms Agreement&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.7pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;In connection with the Notes Purchase Agreement (see note 7(b)) and the New Credit Agreement (see note 7(c)), the Company entered into a Common Terms Agreement with the lenders. This agreement sets out certain provisions, conditions, representations and covenants under the Note Purchase Agreement and Credit Agreement. The Common Terms Agreement requires compliance with affirmative and negative covenants, including, among other things, financial statement reporting requirements and limitations or restrictions relating to the use of the proceeds, additional indebtedness and disposition of assets. The Company was in compliance with all covenants at December&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;As of December 31, 2025, minimum principal payments under the Company's financing arrangements for the next five years are as follows (in thousands):&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 93%; margin-left: 22.2pt; border-collapse: collapse" class="e-rte-table"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 11.5pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 31.84%; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 3.86%; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 10.84%; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 1.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -1.25pt; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 2.54%; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 1.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -1.25pt; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 10.84%; border-bottom: 0