        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-1957_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-1957_336153_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-621_336105_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Represents proceeds from the disposal of fixed assets.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-642_336107_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p>The amount reported on Page 200, Line 21, Column (c) contains both Amortization of Transmission Plant and Amortization of Intangible Plant as shown in the table below. </p><p>  1.) $2,949,563 Amortization of Transmission Plant<br />   2.) $1,447,207 Amortization of General Plant<br />   3.) $4,028,759 Amortization of Intangible Plant<br />   4.) $0 Amortization of Other Utility Plant (Page 200, Line 21, Column (c)) </p><p>Transmission Accumulated Depreciation is reported on Page 219, Line 25, Column (c) <br />   5.) $26,804,185 Transmission Accumulated Depreciation (Page 219, Line 25, Column (c))</p><p>General Depreciation is reported on Page 219, Line 28, Column (c)<br />   6.) $594,723 General Depreciation (Page 219, Line 28, Column (c))</p><p>For Appendix A, Page 2, Line 13 (Transmission Accumulated Depreciation) of the Company's formula rate, the Company uses the sum of the Transmission items in 1.) and 5.) above. For the 2025 Annual Update, refer to Attachment 2, Line 90 for the December 2025 values and derivation of the 13-month average used on Appendix A. </p><p>For Appendix A, Page 2, Line 15 (General and Intangible Accumulated Depreciation) of the Company's formula rate, the Company uses the sum of the General and Intangible items in 2.), 3.) and 6.) above. For the 2025 Annual Update, refer to Attachment 2, Lines 120 and 135 for the December 2025 values and derivation of the 13-month average used on Appendix A. <br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-860_336108_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Represents the amount transferred from FERC account 303 to 351.2 and 397.2 as a result of FERC Order 898.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-922_336109_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Represents the amount transferred from FERC account 391 to 351.1 and 397.1 as a result of FERC Order 898.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-936_336110_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Represents the amount transferred from FERC account 397.3 to 351.3 as a result of FERC Order 898.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-948_336111_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Date Expected to be used in Utility Service: 2026 - 2028<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1002_336113_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p>The amount reported on Page 200, Line 21, Column (c) contains both Amortization of Transmission Plant and Amortization of Intangible Plant as shown in the table below. </p><p>  1.) $2,949,563 Amortization of Transmission Plant<br />   2.) $1,447,207 Amortization of General Plant<br />   3.) $4,028,759 Amortization of Intangible Plant<br />   4.) $0 Amortization of Other Utility Plant (Page 200, Line 21, Column (c)) </p><p>Transmission Accumulated Depreciation is reported on Page 219, Line 25, Column (c) <br />   5.) $26,804,185 Transmission Accumulated Depreciation (Page 219, Line 25, Column (c))</p><p>General Depreciation is reported on Page 219, Line 28, Column (c)<br />   6.) $594,723 General Depreciation (Page 219, Line 28, Column (c))</p><p>For Appendix A, Page 2, Line 13 (Transmission Accumulated Depreciation) of the Company's formula rate, the Company uses the sum of the Transmission items in 1.) and 5.) above. For the 2025 Annual Update, refer to Attachment 2, Line 90 for the December 2025 values and derivation of the 13-month average used on Appendix A. </p><p>For Appendix A, Page 2, Line 15 (General and Intangible Accumulated Depreciation) of the Company's formula rate, the Company uses the sum of the General and Intangible items in 2.), 3.) and 6.) above. For the 2025 Annual Update, refer to Attachment 2, Lines 120 and 135 for the December 2025 values and derivation of the 13-month average used on Appendix A. <br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1007_336112_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Represents the amount transferred from FERC account 111 to 108 as a result of FERC Order 898.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1128_336115_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p>During 2025, the Company transferred $2,062,795 previously recorded in FERC account 211 to 236 to conform with the current presentation of income tax accruals. As reflected on page 262-263, the cash payment of $2,062,795 represents the settlement of income tax obligations with the parent company. The FERC account 236 year-end balance of $1,874,146 reported on page 112, line 42 represents the current income taxes payable to the parent company. </p><p>The Company is a member of an affiliated group that files a consolidated federal income tax return. Income taxes are allocated to the Company based on a separate return methodology. The Company does not remit income taxes directly to taxing authorities. Instead, amounts are settled through intercompany balances with the parent company. For financial reporting purposes, the Company presents current income tax accruals in FERC account 236. These balances represent obligations to the parent company rather than governmental entities. </p><p><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1174_336116_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>On August 28, 2025, the Company entered into a note purchase agreement and subsequently repaid all outstanding amounts under the Credit Agreement.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1175_336117_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>On August 28, 2025, the Company entered into a note purchase agreement and subsequently repaid all outstanding amounts under the Credit Agreement.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1217_336118_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; line-height: 1.2; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding: 40px; max-width: 850px; margin: auto; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); border: 1px solid rgba(204, 204, 204, 1)">    <div style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 20px">        <h1 style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 0; font-weight: bold"><br /></h1>    </div>    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px">        <h2 style="font-size: 11pt; margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: bold">RECONCILIATION OF REPORTED NET INCOME</h2>        <h2 style="font-size: 11pt; margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: bold">WITH FEDERAL TAXABLE INCOME</h2>    </div>    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10pt" class="e-rte-table">                    <tr>                <td style="width: 30px; vertical-align: top; padding: 2px">1.</td>                <td style="padding: 2px">Net Income per Statement of Income</td>                <td style="text-align: right; width: 120px; padding: 2px">19,922,854</td>            </tr>            <tr><td colspan="3" style="height: 10px"><br /></td></tr>            <tr>                <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 2px">2.</td>                <td style="padding: 2px">Federal Income Taxes</td>                <td style="text-align: right; padding: 2px">5,556,517</td>            </tr>            <tr><td colspan="3" style="height: 10px"><br /></td></tr>            <tr>                <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 2px">3.</td>                <td style="padding: 2px">Excess Capital Loss over Capital Gain</td>                <td style="text-align: right; padding: 2px"><br /></td>            </tr>            <tr><td colspan="3" style="height: 10px"><br /></td></tr>            <tr>             